    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 31a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31a" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hine man æniges þingces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IICn_31a.lnote.oe.25"/> teo, andswarie innan þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> hundrede, þær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#IICn_31a.lnote.oe.26"/> he on beclypod beo, swa hit rihtlagu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#IICn_31a.lnote.oe.27"/> sig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf hine man æniges ðinges téo, andswarie innan ðam hundrede, ðær he on beclypod béo, swa hit lagu séo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31a" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="334" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hine man æniges þingces teo, andswerige innan þam hundre[de<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_31a.lnote.oe.2"/>], þær he on beclepad beo, swa hit rihtlaga sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31a" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si accusetur in aliquo, respondeat in hundreto<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_31a.lnote.oe.9"/>, ubi compellabitur, sicut recta<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_31a.lnote.oe.10"/> lex sit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31a" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis illum accusauerit, secundum legem respondeat in illo centenario, in quo accusatus sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="31a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="192" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf hine man æniges ðinges téo, andswarie innan ðam hundrede ðær he on beclypod béo, swa hit lagu<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_31a.robnote.fn.5"/> séo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="272" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif hine man æniges þingces teo, andswarie innan þam hundrede, þær he on beclypod beo, swa hit rihtlagu sig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="335" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn der [Hauseinwohner<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_31a.lnote.de.1"/>] irgend einer Sache angeklagt wird, antworte er innerhalb dieser Hundertschaft, wo er angeklagt wird, wie es ordentliche Rechtssatzung ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if [the household man] is accused of anything, let him answer within the hundred in which he is accused, as is the proper law.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="193" ed="#robertson"/>And if any accusation is brought against one of them, he shall answer [it], in accordance with the law, within the hundred in which he is accused.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="466" ed="#whitelock"/>And if he<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_31a.whinote.n.4"/> is accused of anything, he is to answer within the hundred, where he is charged, as the true law is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="273" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if an accusation is brought against any of them, he is to answer it in the appropriate hundred, just as the law decrees.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_52">Leis Wl 52</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 335, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">rihtlagu: lagu B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">resp. in i. c., in q. a. sit, sec. leg. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">resp. in i. c., in q. a. sit, sec. leg. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">suo <hi rend="italic">fügt zu K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">K adds suo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">335</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">l. r. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">l. r. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">334</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðinges t., answerige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðinges t., answerige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">334</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þære he on becleopad <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þære he on becleopad Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">334</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ga sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ga sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">334</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hundre <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hundre A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_31a.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">207</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘his man’ Price-Thorpe zu weit. Nicht ‘der Herr’, wie Schmid versteht, laut Stellung zwischen zwei Haushalt betreffenden Sätzen und laut der Quelle. Der Satz will vermutlich das ordentliche Hundred (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 32) zuständig erhalten auch über Gefolge (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 16) des Adels gegen Übergriff privater Gerichtsbarkeit; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 29c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘his man’ Price-Thorpe, too wide. Not ‘the lord’, as Schmid understands it, in view of its position between two sentences concerning the household and in view of the source. The sentence is presumably meant to keep the ordinary hundred (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word, 32) competent over the retinue (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 16) of the nobility too, against encroachment by private jurisdiction; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 29c</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_31a.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">192</biblScope></bibl><label>lagu</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">rihtlagu</hi> (<hi rend="italic">-a</hi>) G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_31a.whinote.n.4" n="4" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">466</biblScope></bibl><label>he</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">any man of the household</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
